ting basal metabolic rate, new standards and review of previous work</article-title><source>Hum Nutr Clin Nutr</source><year>1985</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4044297</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Conway</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Seale</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>DR</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Irwin</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Ainsworth</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of energy expenditure estimates from doubly labeled water, a physical activity questionnaire, and physical activity records</article-title><source>American Journal of Clinical Nutrition</source><year>2002</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>519</fpage><lpage>525</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11864858</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spadano</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Must</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bandini</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name><name><surname>Dallal</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dietz</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Energy cost of physical activities in 12-y-old girls: MET values and influence of body weight</article-title><source>International Journal of Obesity and Related Metabolic Disorders</source><year>2003</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>1528</fpage><lpage>1553</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14634685</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.ijo.0802440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ta